INSERT INTO "prompt_templates" ("name","description","variables","content","slug","id","inserted_at","updated_at") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) ["E2E Behavioral Review Dispatch Prompt", "Sent when a task is in_review and one or more pending validations are `e2e_behavior`. Walks the review agent through executing each planner-authored adversarial test case in a worktree dev server, then dispositioning each validation independently.", ["task_title", "pending_e2e_validations_json", "execution_space_id", "repo_url", "task_slug", "federation_preamble", "feedback_guidance"], "Task is in behavioral review — execute each planner-authored e2e_behavior test case and disposition each validation independently.\n\nTask: {{task_title}}\nExecution space: {{execution_space_id}}\nRepository: {{repo_url}}\nTask slug: {{task_slug}}\n\n## What is e2e_behavior\n\nThe planner authored an adversarial test plan (a list of `e2e_behavior` validations) describing\nwhat user-visible behavior must hold for this task to be considered done. Each validation is one\nindependently-dispositioned test case. Your job is to execute every test case in a running dev\nenvironment and report pass/fail per validation with concrete evidence.\n\n## Pending e2e_behavior validations (pre-rendered as JSON)\n\nYou have one or more pending e2e_behavior validations on this task. Each entry below carries a\n`validation_id` and an `evaluation_payload`. Run each one in turn.\n\n```\n{{pending_e2e_validations_json}}\n```\n\nEach `evaluation_payload` contains three fields:\n- `setup`: prepare the dev environment (fixtures, seeds, etc.)\n- `actions`: concrete steps to perform against the running feature\n- `expected`: the observable behavior that constitutes success\n\nThere is no planner-supplied `failure_feedback` — on a failed verdict, you (the review agent) compose the\nfeedback yourself from what you actually observed. That is the failure_feedback.\n\n## How to review\n\n1. Start a worktree dev server for this task — reference the `suite-dev-server` skill from the bundled skills payload. The skill explains the dev host's constraints and DB seeding.\n2. For each pending validation in the list above:\n   a. Perform the `setup` steps from its payload (creating fixtures via Burrow MCP tools or DB seeds, depending on what the script asks for).\n   b. Perform the `actions` against the running feature.\n   c. Compare the observed behavior to `expected`.\n   d. Disposition that single validation (see below) before moving to the next test case. Failures on one validation do NOT short-circuit the rest — run them all.\n\n## Design fidelity (when an Attached design canvases block is present)\n\nA case whose `setup` begins `Fidelity case — canvas <id>` is a fidelity case. Render canvases with the recipe in this dispatch's Attached design canvases block.\n\nTwo kinds of design canvas. Tell them apart by the title and the node types, never by the canvas `kind` field: `kind` is the root node type and is `stack` for nearly every canvas.\n- **Prototype or mockup canvas** (contains a `prototype` or `embed` node): it IS the spec, matched screen for screen.\n- **Design-direction canvas** (titled `Design direction: …`, or containing no `embed` and no `prototype` node; the title prefix wins): it records intent only. Check the presence of the elements, states, copy and token slots it names, NOT layout resemblance to its wireframes. The side-by-side is context; only the inventory check gates.\n\nFor each fidelity case:\n1. Render the canvas with the block's recipe AND the implementation on the worktree dev server, at the SAME viewport(s) the case names.\n2. Upload both screenshots with `attachment_upload_start` and a curl POST of the bytes. Create an evidence canvas in the execution space with `canvas_create`: a `row` of two `card`s, `Design` and `Implementation`, each holding an `image` node whose `src` is `/chat/attachments/<uuid>`. Post its link to the execution space.\n3. Check every inventory row MECHANICALLY where possible: a DOM query for each verbatim string, a selector-presence check for each element and state. Record a per-row present/missing table. A `missing` row counts only after a positive control in the same session shows the same query finds a known-present string on that page.\n4. Read the executor's `Design deviations — stage <n>` posts in the execution space. A declared deviation is recorded in the evidence and does not by itself fail the case. A missing inventory row, changed copy, or (prototype or mockup canvas only) structure that is in neither the inventory nor the declarations FAILS the case.\n5. The evidence map carries `side_by_side_canvas_id`, `inventory_results` (the per-row table) and " <> ..., "dispatch.review_e2e", "01a18f2c-95e0-7001-9be7-f1f0f1dd817b", ~U[2026-10-30 23:37:06.272914Z], ~U[2026-10-30 23:37:06.272914Z]]

