INSERT INTO "prompt_templates" ("name","description","variables","content","slug","id","inserted_at","updated_at") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) ["Scribe Completion Dispatch Prompt", "Sent to the scribe agent on `meeting_scribe_completion` attention signals. Instructs the scribe to produce a 5-card meeting summary canvas (Summary / Decisions / Action items / Open questions / Provenance) in the meeting's chat space and hand structured action items off to the triage agent via `meeting_scribe_complete`. Codifies the Globex scribe canvas structure proven on the 2026-07-13 meeting.", ["space_id", "room_id", "transcript_id", "meeting_name", "execution_space_id", "federation_preamble", "skills_reference", "meeting_id", "run_id", "snapshot_hash", "canvas_id", "source_transcript_ids", "accepted_action_candidates", "completion_transcript"], "{{federation_preamble}}\n\n## This run — every identifier is in this message, not the tag attributes\n\n- meeting_id={{meeting_id}}, run_id={{run_id}}, transcript_id={{transcript_id}}, snapshot_hash={{snapshot_hash}}\n- canvas_id={{canvas_id}} (blank on the first run means canvas_create; otherwise update that canvas)\n- source_transcript_ids={{source_transcript_ids}}\n\nComplete this step by calling the MCP tool `meeting_scribe_complete` with meeting_id={{meeting_id}}, run_id={{run_id}}, transcript_id={{transcript_id}}, snapshot_hash={{snapshot_hash}} and the canvas_id you created.\n\n### Accepted action candidates\n\n{{accepted_action_candidates}}\n\n### Full finalized transcript (segment_id | time | speaker: text)\n\n{{completion_transcript}}\n\nMeeting `{{meeting_name}}` just ended — produce the 5-card scribe completion canvas.\n\n## Signal payload — read these from the attention signal\n\n- `space_id={{space_id}}` — the meeting's chat space; create the canvas here.\n- `room_id={{room_id}}` — the LiveKit room the meeting occupied.\n- `transcript_id={{transcript_id}}` — durable transcript reference for `memory_search` filters.\n- `execution_space_id={{execution_space_id}}` — your working space for evidence + status updates.\n\nRead `meeting_id`, `run_id`, `snapshot_hash`, `completion_transcript` and\n`source_transcript_ids` from the `This run` block above. `completion_transcript` is the full\nordered segment snapshot across the meeting's recordings. Use it, not the latest chunk\nor summary alone. Preserve these canonical identities unchanged in the callback.\nUse `space_get_context` for supporting context only. No task or stage ack is needed.\nIf the signal has a canvas_id, update that existing canvas and preserve action checklist\nnode ids for the same work. Do not create a replacement canvas or mint new item ids.\nOnly the first run without canvas_id uses canvas_create. This rule overrides the\nsingle canvas_create instruction below on a refreshed snapshot.\n\n## Deliverable — ONE canvas in `space_id={{space_id}}` with five cards\n\nEmit the canvas via a single `canvas_create` call rooted at a `stack` containing five `card`\nnodes in the order below. Do NOT split into multiple canvases. Use `heading` + `markdown` nodes\ninside cards for prose, and a `checklist` node for the action-items card.\n\n### Card 1 — Summary\n\nMeeting metadata + a two-to-four sentence narrative. Include:\n\n- Meeting name (`{{meeting_name}}`), date, wall-clock duration.\n- Participant list (resolved `user:*` identities where possible). If any identity is ambiguous\n  — e.g. the transcriber heard \"Sam\" but the participant roster has both `user:sam` and\n  `user:saru` on the invite (as on the Globex 2026-07-13 meeting) — flag it inline: \"attributed\n  to Sam/Saru — transcriber cannot disambiguate\".\n- Transcript stats: rough turn count, total words (from the transcript summary if available).\n- Mishearing corrections applied — call out every proper-noun or hostname you corrected from the raw transcript.\n\n### Card 2 — Decisions\n\nBulleted list. One decision per bullet in the form:\n\n`**<decision in one sentence>** — decided by <owner>; \"<load-bearing quote from transcript>\"`\n\nPrefer quotes short enough to sit inline (under 200 chars). If no clear decision emerged,\nwrite \"No durable decisions recorded this meeting.\" — do NOT invent decisions to fill the card.\n\n### Card 3 — Action items\n\nUse an `actions` checklist whose children are `checklist_item` nodes. Give every item a\nstable node `id`; triage uses that exact id as `item_id` across retries. Include grounded\ndescriptions and `source_segment_ids` from `completion_transcript` in the note. Separate\nquestions and canvas edits from concrete follow-up work; do not turn transcript comments\ninto tasks. For each action item:\n\n- `label` — human-readable: `<owner>: <action verb + object> <due-hint>`\n  Example: `\"Alex: draft the Globex Q3 pricing memo by Friday\"`.\n- `note` — **structured JSON** (a stringified JSON object, not prose) with the exact keys\n  below. All keys required; use `null` for any field you cannot determine from the transcript.\n\nJSON schema" <> ..., "dispatch.scribe_completion", "01a18f2c-95e2-7000-8b80-09c22bb28c3a", ~U[2026-10-30 23:37:06.274268Z], ~U[2026-10-30 23:37:06.274268Z]]

